[data-can-leave] Anything this agent reads — $ROOT/home/Documents/research and whatever your BRAVE_SEARCH_KEY unlocks on api.search.brave.com — can be sent to api.search.brave.com (acting as you) and any public hostname. The fetch tool's GET requests are not prompted and can carry data out in the URL.
This agent:
- uses a model you pick at launch.
- can read $ROOT/home/Documents/research (at /workspace/research); can write there with your approval; cannot delete there.
- can reach api.search.brave.com on port 443, any public hostname on port 443 (through the Sallyport proxy only).
- uses your BRAVE_SEARCH_KEY secret only toward api.search.brave.com (the agent never sees the value).
- cannot run shell commands.
- fetch can only read (GET/HEAD) without your approval.
- may call: fs_read, fs_list, fs_write, fetch.
- is limited to 2 CPUs, 4GiB memory, 256 processes, and 2h of wall time.
